+# Contributing to Webbrik
+
+Thanks for helping. Please read this before opening a pull request.
+
+## Ground rules
+- Open an issue first for anything bigger than a small fix, so we agree on the direction before you spend time.
+- Keep changes focused: one fix or feature per pull request, with tests.
+- Run `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm test` before you push. CI runs them again.
+- Follow the existing code style and the visual language in [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md).
+
+## Licence of contributions
+Webbrik is licensed under the [Apache License 2.0](LICENSE). By submitting a contribution you agree that it is licensed under the same terms (Apache 2.0, section 5), and you confirm you have the right to submit it. Sign off each commit to say so:
+
+```bash
+git commit -s -m "Fix the thing"
+```
+
+The sign-off line (`Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@example.com>`) certifies the [Developer Certificate of Origin](https://developercertificate.org/). You keep the copyright in your own contribution. The project owner keeps the copyright in the project as a whole and in the Webbrik name and logo.
+
+## Reporting a security problem
+Please do not open a public issue. See [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).
